<h2>Deceleration</h2>

<p><b>One concept:</b> Deceleration occurs when an object''s speed decreases with time.</p>

<h3>What happens during deceleration?</h3>

<p>
Suppose a car is moving at 25 m/s and later moves at 15 m/s.
Its speed has decreased.
</p>

<p>
The change is:
</p>

<p>
15 - 25 = <b>-10 m/s</b>
</p>

<p>
The negative result indicates that the velocity has decreased in the
chosen positive direction.
</p>

<h3>Example 1</h3>

<p>
A car slows from 20 m/s to 10 m/s in 5 seconds. Find its acceleration.
</p>

<p><b>Step 1:</b></p>

<p>
u = 20 m/s
</p>

<p>
v = 10 m/s
</p>

<p>
t = 5 s
</p>

<p><b>Step 2:</b> Find the change in velocity.</p>

<p>
v - u = 10 - 20
</p>

<p>
v - u = -10 m/s
</p>

<p><b>Step 3:</b> Divide by time.</p>

<p>
a = -10 / 5
</p>

<p>
a = <b>-2 m/s²</b>
</p>

<h3>Example 2</h3>

<p>
A motorcycle slows from 30 m/s to 18 m/s in 4 seconds.
Find its acceleration.
</p>

<p><b>Step 1:</b></p>

<p>
u = 30 m/s, v = 18 m/s, t = 4 s
</p>

<p><b>Step 2:</b></p>

<p>
v - u = 18 - 30 = -12 m/s
</p>

<p><b>Step 3:</b></p>

<p>
a = -12 / 4
</p>

<p>
a = <b>-3 m/s²</b>
</p>

<h3>Example 3</h3>

<p>
A bus reduces its velocity from 24 m/s to 6 m/s in 6 seconds.
Find its acceleration.
</p>

<p><b>Step 1:</b></p>

<p>
u = 24 m/s, v = 6 m/s, t = 6 s
</p>

<p><b>Step 2:</b></p>

<p>
v - u = 6 - 24 = -18 m/s
</p>

<p><b>Step 3:</b></p>

<p>
a = -18 / 6
</p>

<p>
a = <b>-3 m/s²</b>
</p>

<h3>Important idea</h3>

<p>
In these straight-line examples, a negative acceleration means the
velocity is decreasing in the chosen positive direction.
</p>

<p>
The negative sign is important. Do not remove it automatically.
</p>
