<h2>Interpreting a Horizontal Section of a Distance-Time Graph</h2>

<p><b>One concept:</b> A horizontal section of a distance-time graph means that the distance is not changing while time continues to pass.</p>

<h3>What does a horizontal line mean?</h3>

<p>
On a distance-time graph:
</p>

<ul>
<li>Time is on the horizontal axis.</li>
<li>Distance is on the vertical axis.</li>
</ul>

<p>
If the graph is horizontal, the distance remains constant while time
increases.
</p>

<p>
This means the object is <b>stationary</b>.
</p>

<h3>Example 1</h3>

<p>
A distance-time graph remains at 100 km from 2 hours to 4 hours.
What is happening during this period?
</p>

<p><b>Step 1:</b> At 2 hours, distance = 100 km.</p>

<p><b>Step 2:</b> At 4 hours, distance = 100 km.</p>

<p><b>Step 3:</b> The distance has not changed.</p>

<p>
Therefore, the object has not moved during those 2 hours.
</p>

<p><b>Answer: The object is stationary.</b></p>

<h3>Example 2</h3>

<p>
A graph shows a horizontal section at 250 km between 5 hours and
7 hours.
How long is the object stationary?
</p>

<p><b>Step 1:</b> Starting time = 5 h.</p>

<p><b>Step 2:</b> Ending time = 7 h.</p>

<p><b>Step 3:</b> Find the time difference.</p>

<p>
7 - 5 = <b>2 h</b>
</p>

<p><b>Answer: The object is stationary for 2 hours.</b></p>

<h3>Example 3</h3>

<p>
A horizontal section of a distance-time graph occurs from 3 hours to
3.5 hours.
Find how long the object remains stationary.
</p>

<p><b>Step 1:</b></p>

<p>
Ending time = 3.5 h
</p>

<p>
Starting time = 3 h
</p>

<p><b>Step 2:</b></p>

<p>
Time stationary = 3.5 - 3
</p>

<p>
Time stationary = <b>0.5 h</b>
</p>

<p>
Since 0.5 h = 30 minutes:
</p>

<p><b>Answer: 30 minutes.</b></p>

<h3>Important idea</h3>

<p>
A horizontal distance-time graph does not mean the object travelled
at zero distance for no reason. It means the object''s measured
distance has stayed unchanged while time passes.
</p>

<h3>Common mistake</h3>

<p>
Do not interpret a horizontal distance-time section as increasing
distance. A horizontal line means <b>no change in distance</b>.
</p>
