</p>

<p>
Set:
</p>

<p>
x = 0
</p>

<p>
Then:
</p>

<p>
0 + y = 10
</p>

<p>
Therefore:
</p>

<p>
y = 10
</p>

<p>
The y-intercept is:
</p>

<p>
<b>(0, 10)</b>
</p>

<h3>Worked Example 2</h3>

<p>
Find the y-intercept of:
</p>

<p>
2x + y = 12
</p>

<p>
Set x = 0:
</p>

<p>
2(0) + y = 12
</p>

<p>
y = 12
</p>

<p>
Therefore:
</p>

<p>
<b>(0, 12)</b>
</p>

<h3>Worked Example 3</h3>

<p>
Find the y-intercept of:
</p>

<p>
3x + 2y = 18
</p>

<p>
Set x = 0:
</p>

<p>
3(0) + 2y = 18
</p>

<p>
2y = 18
</p>

<p>
y = 9
</p>

<p>
Therefore:
</p>

<p>
<b>(0, 9)</b>
</p>

<h3>Key rule</h3>

<p>
To find the y-intercept:
</p>

<p>
<b>Set x = 0.</b>
</p>
