<p>
P(A) = 2/6 = 1/3
</p>

<p>
Event B = getting 5.
</p>

<p>
P(B) = 1/6
</p>

<p>
A and B are mutually exclusive.
</p>

<p>
Therefore:
</p>

<p>
P(A or B)
= 1/3 + 1/6
</p>

<p>
Convert 1/3 to sixths:
</p>

<p>
1/3 = 2/6
</p>

<p>
Therefore:
</p>

<p>
2/6 + 1/6
= 3/6
= <b>1/2</b>
