<p>
P(B) = 2/6 = 1/3
</p>

<p>
The events are mutually exclusive.
</p>

<p>
Therefore:
</p>

<p>
P(A or B)
= 1/2 + 1/3
</p>

<p>
Using a common denominator of 6:
</p>

<p>
1/2 = 3/6
</p>

<p>
1/3 = 2/6
</p>

<p>
Therefore:
</p>

<p>
3/6 + 2/6
= 5/6
