<h2>Solving Matrix Equations</h2> <p> A matrix equation can contain an unknown matrix. The aim is to isolate the unknown matrix. </p> <h3>Worked Example 1</h3> <p><b>Question:</b> Find X if:</p> <pre> X + [ 2 3 4 5 ] = [ 7 9 10 12 ] </pre> <p> We need X by itself. The matrix added to X must therefore be removed by subtraction. </p> <pre> X = [ 7 9 10 12 ] - [ 2 3 4 5 ] </pre> <p> Subtract corresponding entries: </p> <pre> 7 - 2 = 5 9 - 3 = 6 10 - 4 = 6 12 - 5 = 7 </pre> <p> Therefore: </p> <pre> X = [ 5 6 6 7 ] </pre> <h3>Worked Example 2</h3> <p><b>Question:</b> Find X if:</p> <pre> 3X = [ 12 15 9 18 ] </pre> <p> Every entry of X has been multiplied by 3. Therefore divide every entry by 3. </p> <pre> 12 ÷ 3 = 4 15 ÷ 3 = 5 9 ÷ 3 = 3 18 ÷ 3 = 6 </pre> <p> Therefore: </p> <pre> X = [ 4 5 3 6 ] </pre> <h3>Worked Example 3</h3> <p><b>Question:</b> Find X if:</p> <pre> X - [ 3 1 2 4 ] = [ 5 7 8 6 ] </pre> <p> The matrix is being subtracted from X. To undo subtraction, add the same matrix to both sides. </p> <pre> X = [ 5 7 8 6 ] + [ 3 1 2 4 ] </pre> <p> Calculate each position: </p> <pre> 5 + 3 = 8 7 + 1 = 8 8 + 2 = 10 6 + 4 = 10 </pre> <p> Therefore: </p> <pre> X = [ 8 8 10 10 ] </pre> <h3>Worked Example 4</h3> <p><b>Question:</b> Find x and y if:</p> <pre> [ x 4 7 y ] + [ 3 2 1 5 ] = [ 8 6 8 12 ] </pre> <h4>Find x</h4> <p> Look at the top-left position. </p> <pre> x + 3 = 8 </pre> <p> Subtract 3: </p> <pre> x = 5 </pre> <h4>Find y</h4> <p> Look at the bottom-right position. </p> <pre> y + 5 = 12 </pre> <p> Subtract 5: </p> <pre> y = 7 </pre> <p> Therefore: </p> <pre> x = 5 y = 7 </pre> <h3>Common Mistake</h3> <p> Always compare entries occupying the same position. Do not compare numbers simply because they appear in the same row or column. </p> ', 1),
