<p><b>Step 2:</b> Mucus traps dust and microorganisms.</p>

<p><b>Step 3:</b> Trapping these particles helps protect deeper parts
of the respiratory system.</p>

<p><b>Answer:</b> Goblet cells produce mucus that traps particles and
microorganisms, helping protect the respiratory tract.</p>
