<h2>Organ System</h2>

<h3>What is an organ system?</h3>

<p>
An <b>organ system</b> is a group of organs that work together to
perform a major function in an organism.
</p>

<h3>Example: digestive system</h3>

<p>
The digestive system contains several organs that work together to
process food and absorb nutrients.
</p>

<p>
The organs have different jobs, but their functions are coordinated
to achieve the overall function of the system.
</p>

<h3>Why are organ systems useful?</h3>

<p>
Complex organisms need many different processes to happen at the same
time. Organ systems allow specialised organs to cooperate.
</p>

<h3>Worked example</h3>

<p><b>Question:</b> Why is the digestive system called an organ system?</p>

<p><b>Step 1:</b> It contains multiple organs.</p>

<p><b>Step 2:</b> These organs perform different parts of digestion
and nutrient processing.</p>

<p><b>Step 3:</b> Their activities work together to achieve a common
overall function.</p>

<p><b>Answer:</b> It is an organ system because several organs work
together to process food and absorb nutrients.</p>
