<p><b>Question:</b> Why is producing more cells useful when an organism
grows?</p>

<p><b>Step 1:</b> Growth requires an increase in the amount of living
material.</p>

<p><b>Step 2:</b> Cell division increases the number of cells.</p>

<p><b>Step 3:</b> The new cells can specialise and become part of tissues.</p>

<p><b>Answer:</b> Cell division increases cell number, allowing the
organism to grow and develop.</p>
