<p><b>Step 2:</b> A cleavage furrow develops.</p>
<p><b>Step 3:</b> The furrow deepens.</p>
<p><b>Step 4:</b> Two separate daughter cells form.</p>

<h3>Key idea</h3>
<p>
The cleavage furrow is the physical process that helps separate the cytoplasm
of an animal cell.
