<p><b>Question:</b> A cell is observed with chromosomes arranged across the middle of
the cell. Which stage is it in?</p>

<p><b>Step 1:</b> Look at the chromosome position.</p>
<p><b>Step 2:</b> They are arranged at the equator.</p>
<p><b>Step 3:</b> Chromosomes at the equator identify metaphase.</p>

<p><b>Answer:</b> Metaphase.</p>

<h3>Order to remember</h3>
<p>
<b>P → M → A → T → C</b>
</p>
<p>
Prophase → Metaphase → Anaphase → Telophase → Cytokinesis
