The palisade cell is positioned close to the upper surface of the leaf,
where it receives plenty of light.
</p>

<p>
It also has many chloroplasts, increasing its ability to absorb light.
</p>

<h3>Worked example</h3>

<p><b>Question:</b> Why does a palisade mesophyll cell contain many chloroplasts?</p>

<p><b>Step 1:</b> The function of the cell is mainly photosynthesis.</p>

<p><b>Step 2:</b> Photosynthesis requires light energy.</p>

<p><b>Step 3:</b> Chloroplasts contain chlorophyll, which absorbs light.</p>

<p><b>Answer:</b> It contains many chloroplasts so that it can absorb more
light energy and carry out photosynthesis efficiently.</p>
