<h2>Cohesion and Adhesion in Water Transport</h2>

<h3>DEEP NOTES</h3>

<p>Water has properties that help maintain a continuous column of water inside xylem vessels.</p>

<h3>Cohesion</h3>

<p><strong>Cohesion</strong> is the attraction between water molecules.</p>

<p>Because water molecules attract one another, they tend to remain connected as a continuous column.</p>

<h3>Adhesion</h3>

<p><strong>Adhesion</strong> is the attraction between water molecules and the walls of the xylem vessel.</p>

<p>Adhesion helps water interact with the vessel walls.</p>

