<h2>Guard Cells</h2>

<h3>DEEP NOTES</h3>

<p><strong>Guard cells</strong> are specialised cells surrounding each stoma.</p>

<p>Their main function is to control whether the stomatal pore is open or closed.</p>

<h3>Why Is Control Necessary?</h3>

<p>Plants need carbon dioxide for photosynthesis, but opening stomata also allows water vapour to escape.</p>

<p>The plant therefore needs to balance:</p>

<p><strong>Carbon dioxide entry ↔ water loss.</strong></p>

