  <h3>What does recessive mean?</h3>

  <p>
    In a simple dominant-recessive inheritance model, a <b>recessive
    allele</b> is expressed in the phenotype when two copies of the recessive
    allele are present.
  </p>

  <p>
    A recessive allele is commonly represented using a lowercase letter.
  </p>

  <p>
    For example:
  </p>

  <p>
    <b>a</b> = recessive allele
  </p>

