<h2>Plant Uptake of Nitrate</h2>

<h3>DEEP NOTES</h3>

<p>
Plants need nitrogen to manufacture important nitrogen-containing substances,
including amino acids, proteins and nucleic acids.
</p>

<p>
Plants cannot normally take nitrogen directly from atmospheric nitrogen gas.
Instead, they obtain usable nitrogen compounds from the soil, especially
<strong>nitrate ions</strong>.
