<p>
A useful investigation compares expired air with ordinary atmospheric air.
The two samples should be tested using the same volume of limewater and the
same procedure.
</p>

<h3>CONCLUSION</h3>

<p>
If expired air turns limewater milky more quickly, this provides evidence that
expired air contains more carbon dioxide than ordinary atmospheric air.
