<h2>Gas Exchange and Surface Area to Volume Ratio</h2>

<h3>DEEP NOTES</h3>

<p>
The efficiency of gaseous exchange is related to the amount of exchange
surface available compared with the volume of tissue that requires gases.
</p>

<h3>WHY IS A LARGE SURFACE AREA USEFUL?</h3>

<p>
A large exchange surface provides many sites through which gases can diffuse.
</p>

<p>
For example, the many alveoli in human lungs produce a very large total
surface area.
