<h3>Worked Example</h3>

<p>Seedlings exposed to light from one side bend towards the opening. Seedlings receiving uniform light remain approximately upright.</p>

<p><strong>What conclusion is supported?</strong></p>

<p>Directional light is associated with directional growth of the shoots.</p>

<h3>Evaluation</h3>

<p>Use several seedlings rather than one.</p>

<p>Repeat the experiment.</p>

<p>Measure curvature rather than relying only on words such as "bent a lot."</p>
