      <li><strong>ment:</strong> development, agreement, improvement.</li>
      <li><strong>ough:</strong> though, through, thought. This combination has different pronunciations in different words.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Use patterns, then verify</h3>
    <p>Patterns are guides, not guarantees. When a spelling looks unfamiliar, consider the word family, check the rule and learn irregular forms separately.</p>
