    <h3>Use exclamation marks carefully</h3>
    <p>Too many exclamation marks can make writing seem exaggerated or unprofessional. In formal reports and academic writing, use them only when the context genuinely requires them.</p>

    <h3>Direct speech</h3>
    <p>"''Get out of the way!'' the driver shouted."</p>
    <p>The exclamation mark belongs to the spoken words. It appears inside the quotation marks in this example.</p>
