    <h2>Colons</h2>
    <p>A colon (:) introduces information that explains, illustrates or expands on what comes before it. It is also used to introduce lists in suitable sentence structures.</p>

    <h3>Introducing a list</h3>
    <p>"Bring the following items: a notebook, a pen and a ruler."</p>
    <p>The words before the colon form a complete introduction to the list.</p>

    <h3>Introducing an explanation</h3>
    <p>"The team had one major problem: nobody had checked the equipment."</p>
    <p>The clause after the colon explains the problem.</p>

    <h3>Introducing an example</h3>
    <p>"One habit improves revision: reviewing difficult topics regularly."</p>
