    <h2>Informational Reports</h2>

    <p>An informational report presents verified information about a subject. It helps readers understand a situation without relying on unsupported claims or emotional language.</p>

    <h3>How to write one</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>Use a specific title.</li>
      <li>State the purpose of the report.</li>
      <li>Arrange information under logical headings.</li>
      <li>Use accurate details, examples or figures when available.</li>
      <li>End with a brief conclusion if the assignment requires one.</li>
    </ol>

    <h3>Model informational report</h3>

    <div style="border:1px solid #999;padding:14px;">
      <h3 style="text-align:center;">REPORT ON WATER USE AT GREENFIELD SECONDARY SCHOOL</h3>
      <p><strong>Prepared by:</strong> Environmental Club Secretary</p>
      <p><strong>Date:</strong> 18 September 2026</p>

      <h4>Introduction</h4>
      <p>This report describes how water is used at Greenfield Secondary School and identifies practices that could help reduce wastage.</p>

      <h4>Areas of Water Use</h4>
      <p>Water is used in the kitchen, laboratories, toilets, cleaning activities and school gardens. Learners also use water for drinking and handwashing.</p>

      <h4>Observations</h4>
      <p>During a school inspection, two taps were found dripping after use. Some learners also left taps running while washing containers. Water collection containers were available near the kitchen, but they were not consistently covered.</p>

      <h4>Suggested Improvements</h4>
      <p>The school could repair leaking taps, remind learners to close taps after use and keep stored water covered. A weekly inspection could help identify problems early.</p>

      <h4>Conclusion</h4>
      <p>Regular maintenance and responsible water use could reduce avoidable wastage and improve water management at the school.</p>
    </div>

    <p><strong>Remember:</strong> Do not invent statistics or claim that a survey was conducted if it was not. When figures are supplied by a question, report them accurately.</p>
