    <h2>Notices and Announcements</h2>

    <p>A notice gives readers important information about an event, change, meeting or instruction. An announcement communicates information to a group, either in writing or orally.</p>

    <h3>What to include in a written notice</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Name of the organisation or group, where relevant.</li>
      <li>A clear heading stating the subject.</li>
      <li>Date of the notice.</li>
      <li>Essential details: what, who, when, where and any action required.</li>
      <li>Name or position of the person responsible, when appropriate.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Model notice</h3>

    <div style="border:1px solid #999;padding:14px;">
      <h3 style="text-align:center;">GREENFIELD SECONDARY SCHOOL</h3>
      <h3 style="text-align:center;">NOTICE: ENVIRONMENTAL CLEAN-UP</h3>
      <p><strong>Date:</strong> 14 September 2026</p>

      <p>All members of the Environmental Club are informed that a school clean-up exercise will take place as follows:</p>

      <p><strong>Date of activity:</strong> Saturday, 19 September 2026</p>
      <p><strong>Time:</strong> 8:00 a.m. to 11:00 a.m.</p>
      <p><strong>Meeting point:</strong> School assembly ground</p>

      <p>Members should arrive on time and bring gloves and reusable water bottles. Waste bags will be provided by the club.</p>

      <p>For further information, contact the club secretary.</p>

      <p><strong>Signed:</strong> Club Patron</p>
    </div>

    <h3>Notice or announcement?</h3>
    <p>A written notice can be read later and should contain the necessary details. An oral announcement is delivered to listeners and may be shorter, but it must still communicate the essential information clearly.</p>
  
<hr>

    <h2>Notices and Announcements</h2>

    <p>A notice communicates important information to a specific audience. It should make the purpose, event, date, time, venue and required action easy to identify.</p>

    <h3>Complete example</h3>

    <div class="writing-example">
      <h3>EMBU SECONDARY SCHOOL</h3>
      <h3>NOTICE: INTER-CLASS DEBATE</h3>

      <p><strong>Date issued:</strong> 10 October 2026</p>

      <p>All Form Three students are informed that an inter-class debate will take place as follows:</p>

      <p><strong>Date:</strong> Friday, 16 October 2026</p>
      <p><strong>Time:</strong> 2.00 p.m.</p>
      <p><strong>Venue:</strong> School assembly hall</p>
      <p><strong>Motion:</strong> School uniforms should be compulsory in all schools.</p>

      <p>Students who wish to participate should register with the English teacher by Wednesday, 14 October. Each class should select two speakers and one timekeeper.</p>

      <p>All interested students are encouraged to attend and support their classmates.</p>

      <p><strong>Signed:</strong> Amina Hassan</p>
      <p>Debate Club Secretary</p>
    </div>

    <h3>Why this notice works</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>The heading identifies the event.</li>
      <li>The date, time and venue are easy to locate.</li>
      <li>The notice explains what interested students must do.</li>
      <li>The issuing person is identified.</li>
    </ul>
