    <h2>Meeting Agendas</h2>

    <p>An agenda is an ordered list of matters to be discussed at a meeting. It helps participants prepare and keeps the meeting focused.</p>

    <h3>What an agenda should contain</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Name of the organisation or committee.</li>
      <li>Type of meeting.</li>
      <li>Date, time and venue.</li>
      <li>Items in a logical order.</li>
      <li>Any preparation participants need to complete.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>Common agenda items include opening the meeting, apologies, confirmation of previous minutes, matters arising, new business and the date of the next meeting. Use only the items relevant to the meeting.</p>

    <h3>Model agenda</h3>

    <div style="border:1px solid #999;padding:14px;">
      <h3 style="text-align:center;">GREENFIELD ENVIRONMENTAL CLUB</h3>
      <h3 style="text-align:center;">AGENDA FOR THE MONTHLY MEETING</h3>

      <p><strong>Date:</strong> 16 October 2026</p>
      <p><strong>Time:</strong> 3:30 p.m.</p>
      <p><strong>Venue:</strong> Science Laboratory</p>

      <ol>
        <li>Opening and welcome</li>
        <li>Apologies for absence</li>
        <li>Confirmation of the previous meeting''s minutes</li>
        <li>Matters arising from the previous minutes</li>
        <li>Planning the school clean-up exercise</li>
        <li>Allocation of duties and materials</li>
        <li>Any other business</li>
        <li>Date of the next meeting</li>
        <li>Adjournment</li>
      </ol>

      <p><strong>Prepared by:</strong> Club Secretary</p>
    </div>

    <p>An agenda lists matters for discussion; it does not record decisions that have already been made. Those belong in the minutes.</p>
  
<hr>

    <h2>Meeting Agendas</h2>

    <p>An agenda is a planned list of matters to be discussed at a meeting. It is usually prepared before the meeting and helps participants prepare and use their time effectively.</p>

    <h3>Complete example</h3>

    <div class="writing-example">
      <h3>EMBU SECONDARY SCHOOL READING CLUB</h3>
      <h3>AGENDA FOR THE MEETING ON 15 OCTOBER 2026</h3>

      <p><strong>Time:</strong> 3.30 p.m.</p>
      <p><strong>Venue:</strong> School library</p>
      <p><strong>Chairperson:</strong> Kevin Mwangi</p>

      <ol>
        <li>Opening and apologies</li>
        <li>Confirmation of the previous meeting''s minutes</li>
        <li>Matters arising from the previous minutes</li>
        <li>Preparation for the reading day</li>
        <li>Allocation of duties and resources</li>
        <li>Any other business</li>
        <li>Date of the next meeting</li>
        <li>Adjournment</li>
      </ol>

      <p><strong>Prepared by:</strong> Amina Hassan, Secretary</p>
      <p><strong>Date prepared:</strong> 10 October 2026</p>
    </div>

    <h3>Agenda versus minutes</h3>
    <p>An agenda lists matters to be discussed before or at the start of a meeting. Minutes record what was discussed and decided after the meeting.</p>
