    <h2>Clear Instructions</h2>

    <p>Instructions explain how to complete a task safely and correctly. They should be arranged in the order in which actions need to happen.</p>

    <h3>Rules for effective instructions</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>State the task or purpose clearly.</li>
      <li>Use direct action verbs such as open, place, check and submit.</li>
      <li>Number steps when order matters.</li>
      <li>Include necessary materials, conditions or warnings.</li>
      <li>Make each step specific enough to follow.</li>
      <li>Use simple, unambiguous language.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Model instructions</h3>

    <div style="border:1px solid #999;padding:14px;">
      <h3>HOW TO SUBMIT AN ASSIGNMENT THROUGH THE SCHOOL PORTAL</h3>

      <p><strong>Before you begin:</strong> Make sure your assignment file is saved in an accepted format and that you can access your school account.</p>

      <ol>
        <li>Open the school''s learning portal in your browser.</li>
        <li>Sign in using your school account.</li>
        <li>Open the subject and select the relevant assignment.</li>
        <li>Read the submission instructions and check the deadline.</li>
        <li>Select the upload option and choose the correct assignment file.</li>
        <li>Wait for the upload to finish.</li>
        <li>Select Submit, if the portal requires a separate submission step.</li>
        <li>Check the confirmation message or submission status before leaving the page.</li>
      </ol>

      <p><strong>Important:</strong> Uploading a file does not always mean it has been submitted. Follow the portal''s final submission procedure.</p>
    </div>

    <p>Good instructions do not assume the reader already knows a critical step. Include warnings where a mistake could cause data loss, safety problems or an unsuccessful submission.</p>
