    <h2>Proposals</h2>

    <p>A proposal presents a plan and asks a person or organisation to approve, support or fund it. A strong proposal explains the need, recommends a practical solution and shows how the plan could be carried out.</p>

    <h3>Common sections</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>Title</li>
      <li>Background or statement of the problem</li>
      <li>Objectives or intended results</li>
      <li>Proposed activities</li>
      <li>Resources and estimated budget, when required</li>
      <li>Expected benefits</li>
      <li>Conclusion or request for approval</li>
    </ol>

    <h3>Complete model proposal</h3>
    <div style="border:1px solid #999;padding:14px;">
      <h3 style="text-align:center;">PROPOSAL TO ESTABLISH A SCHOOL READING CORNER</h3>
      <p><strong>Submitted to:</strong> The Principal, Greenfield Secondary School</p>
      <p><strong>Submitted by:</strong> English Club</p>
      <p><strong>Date:</strong> 19 October 2026</p>

      <h4>1. Background</h4>
      <p>Some learners need a quiet space where they can read supplementary books during free periods. The English Club proposes establishing a small reading corner in an unused section of the library.</p>

      <h4>2. Objectives</h4>
      <ul>
        <li>Encourage regular independent reading.</li>
        <li>Make suitable supplementary reading materials easier to access.</li>
        <li>Promote responsible sharing and care of books.</li>
      </ul>

      <h4>3. Proposed Activities</h4>
      <p>The club will identify suitable books, arrange donated materials by category, prepare a borrowing record and create a rota for keeping the area tidy.</p>

      <h4>4. Resources Required</h4>
      <p>The project will need two small shelves, labels, a register and donated books. The school will be asked to provide the space and approve any necessary purchases. Costs will be confirmed after obtaining quotations.</p>

      <h4>5. Expected Benefits</h4>
      <p>The reading corner is expected to give learners easier access to supplementary reading and encourage a stronger reading culture.</p>

      <h4>6. Conclusion</h4>
      <p>The English Club requests approval to establish the reading corner and permission to collect suitable book donations. The club will report on its progress after the first term of operation.</p>

      <p><strong>Signed:</strong> English Club Chairperson</p>
    </div>

    <p>A proposal should not present estimated results as guaranteed outcomes. Any budget should use realistic figures supported by quotations or clearly labelled estimates.</p>
  
<hr>

    <h2>Proposals</h2>

    <p>A proposal presents a suggested project or course of action for consideration. It explains the need, the proposed activities, the resources required and how success could be evaluated. Follow the format requested by the organisation.</p>

    <h3>Complete example: School Reading Day Proposal</h3>

    <div class="writing-example">
      <h3>PROPOSAL FOR A SCHOOL READING DAY</h3>
      <p><strong>Prepared by:</strong> School Reading Club</p>
      <p><strong>Date:</strong> 10 October 2026</p>

      <h4>1. Background</h4>
      <p>The reading club proposes a school reading day to encourage regular reading and give students opportunities to discuss books they enjoy.</p>

      <h4>2. Purpose</h4>
      <p>The event is intended to increase student participation in reading activities and provide a platform for students to share book recommendations.</p>

      <h4>3. Proposed Activities</h4>
      <ol>
        <li>A thirty-minute individual reading session.</li>
        <li>Small-group discussions about selected books.</li>
        <li>Short student presentations recommending a book.</li>
        <li>A display of books available in the school library.</li>
      </ol>

      <h4>4. Resources Required</h4>
      <ul>
        <li>Access to the school library or an approved classroom.</li>
        <li>Books and writing materials.</li>
        <li>Teacher supervision.</li>
        <li>Noticeboard space for the programme.</li>
      </ul>

      <h4>5. Proposed Date and Schedule</h4>
      <p>The club proposes 24 October 2026, from 9.00 a.m. to 12.00 noon, subject to approval and venue availability.</p>

      <h4>6. Estimated Budget</h4>
      <p>Printing notices: KSh 300.</p>
      <p>Stationery: KSh 500.</p>
      <p><strong>Estimated total: KSh 800.</strong></p>
      <p>These figures are planning estimates and should be confirmed before approval.</p>

      <h4>7. Evaluation</h4>
      <p>The club will record attendance, collect brief participant feedback and review the number of students who volunteer to join future reading activities.</p>

      <h4>8. Request for Approval</h4>
      <p>We request permission to hold the event and to use the proposed venue. We welcome any adjustments the school administration considers necessary.</p>

      <p>Prepared by:</p>
      <p>Kevin Mwangi</p>
      <p>Secretary, School Reading Club</p>
    </div>
