  (6471, 1596, 'A seedling increases from 3 cm at Day 2 to 9 cm at Day 5. Calculate the gradient.', 'text', 1, 'Focus on the core principle of plant_growth_graph_gradient.', '{"why":"(9 − 3) ÷ (5 − 2) = 6 ÷ 3 = 2 cm/day.","sol":"Step 1: Identify key concept: Define the required principles for plant_growth_graph_gradient.\nStep 2: Apply governing rule: (9 − 3) ÷ (5 − 2) = 6 ÷ 3 = 2 cm/day.\nStep 3: State the final conclusion: 2 cm/day","steps":["Step 1: Identify key concept: Define the required principles for plant_growth_graph_gradient.","Step 2: Apply governing rule: (9 − 3) ÷ (5 − 2) = 6 ÷ 3 = 2 cm/day.","Step 3: State the final conclusion: 2 cm/day"],"options":[],"conceptId":"biology_plant_growth_and_development_plant_growth_graph_gradient","skillId":"biology_plant_growth_and_development","subskillId":"biology_plant_growth_and_development_q2","subject":"biology","chapter":"plant_growth_and_development","topic":"plant_growth_graph_gradient"}', 1),
