  (4258, 3208, 'Metallic bonding is the strong electrostatic attraction between positive metal ions and delocalised electrons.', TRUE),
  (4259, 3209, 'Sodium contributes its one outer electron to the delocalised electron system and forms Na⁺. Electrostatic attraction between Na⁺ ions and the delocalised electrons holds the structure together.', TRUE),
