  (4262, 3212, 'Strong electrostatic attraction between positive metal ions and delocalised electrons holds the structure together.', TRUE),
  (4263, 3213, 'A delocalised electron is an electron that is not confined to one particular atom and can move throughout the metallic structure.', TRUE),
