  (4268, 3218, 'Metals conduct electricity because mobile delocalised electrons carry electric charge through the structure when a potential difference is applied.', TRUE),
  (4269, 3219, 'Malleability is the ability to be hammered into sheets. Metals are malleable because layers of ions can shift while the delocalised electrons continue to attract the positive ions.', TRUE),
