  (5150, 4100, 'Strength describes the extent of ionisation, while concentration describes how much acid is present per volume of solution. Sulphuric acid can be strong yet dilute.', TRUE),
  (5151, 4101, 'Slowly add acid to water while stirring and wearing appropriate protective equipment. Never pour water into concentrated acid because rapid heating can cause dangerous splashing.', TRUE),
  (5152, 4102, 'It means concentrated sulphuric acid can remove water from certain substances, sometimes causing substantial chemical changes.', TRUE),
