  (5457, 4407, 'Complete combustion occurs with sufficient oxygen and produces carbon dioxide and water. Incomplete combustion occurs with insufficient oxygen and may produce carbon monoxide and/or carbon, as well as water.', TRUE),
  (5458, 4408, '2C(s) + O₂(g) → 2CO(g). Carbon monoxide is poisonous because it reduces the blood''s ability to transport oxygen.', TRUE),
  (5459, 4409, 'The claim is incorrect. Complete combustion produces carbon dioxide and water: CH₄ + 2O₂ → CO₂ + 2H₂O.', TRUE),
  (5460, 4410, 'It can produce poisonous carbon monoxide and soot or carbon particles that contribute to air pollution and health problems.', TRUE),
